  "notes": "West leads the ♦5 against 6♥. With an almost certain trump loser, the diamond finesse represents the best chance of making the contract. Accordingly, South should finesse North's ♦Q at trick 1.\n\nWhen East wins the ♦K and returns a diamond, South must play the heart suit for no losers. There is only one hope. One of the defenders must hold doubleton Queen and Jack of hearts. The ♥A and ♥K will drop the ♥Q and ♥J. The ♥10 will then be high and it can be used to draw the last trump.\n\nWhen South leads a small heart off the dummy and East follows with the ♥Q or ♥J, South should not be tempted to finesse the ♥9 on the second round. If East was dealt a singleton honour in hearts, West will always have a heart trick. If East was dealt honour doubleton in hearts, he could have guaranteed a defensive heart trick by playing low.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦5 against 6♥. With an almost certain trump loser, the diamond finesse represents the best chance of making the contract. Accordingly, South should finesse North's ♦Q at trick 1.",
    "When East wins the ♦K and returns a diamond, South must play the heart suit for no losers. There is only one hope. One of the defenders must hold doubleton Queen and Jack of hearts. The ♥A and ♥K will drop the ♥Q and ♥J. The ♥10 will then be high and it can be used to draw the last trump.",
    "When South leads a small heart off the dummy and East follows with the ♥Q or ♥J, South should not be tempted to finesse the ♥9 on the second round. If East was dealt a singleton honour in hearts, West will always have a heart trick. If East was dealt honour doubleton in hearts, he could have guaranteed a defensive heart trick by playing low."
  ],
